The flag value of `false` from `MPI_Win_test` indicates that the exposure epoch has **not yet ended**. This means that the synchronization initiated by `MPI_Win_post` and `MPI_Win_start` is still in progress, and any RMA operations on the window may not have completed. 

Your code should **not proceed under the assumption that the exposure epoch has ended** in this case. You must check the `flag` value and only proceed when it is `true`. For example:

```c
int flag;
MPI_Win_test(win, &flag);
if (flag) {
    // Exposure epoch has ended; proceed
} else {
    // Exposure epoch is still active; wait or retry
}
```

This ensures correctness by respecting the synchronization state of the window.

